QR Code Generator
A simple and interactive Python script to generate customized QR codes with custom colors and sizes.

Features
✅ Interactive menu for easy use
✅ Custom colors for QR code and background
✅ Adjustable size with box_size parameter
✅ Automatic display and file saving
✅ Support for any text or URL
Requirements
Install the required packages:

Or:

How to use
1. Run the program
2. Interactive menu
The program presents a simple menu:

1 - Generate QR code
2 - Exit
3. QR code generation
When generating a QR code, you'll be prompted for:

Text/URL: The content to encode
Filename: Output file name (e.g., qr.png)
Size: Box size for each QR module (e.g., 10)
QR Color: Color of the QR code (default: black)
Background Color: Background color (default: white)
Example usage
Color options
You can use any color name supported by PIL:

Standard colors: black, white, red, blue, green, yellow, etc.
Extended colors: darkblue, lightgray, orange, purple, etc.
Hex colors: #FF0000, #00FF00, #0000FF, etc.
RGB tuples: (255, 0, 0), (0, 255, 0), etc.
Project structure
Dependencies
qrcode: QR code generation library
Pillow (PIL): Image processing library
